-- title:
--   Interpolate Completed Slices Restrict At Height Eq Get Of Mem Support Subset
-- statement:
--   **The default eligible interpolation recovers every selected slice.**
--
--   Let `params` have a field model, let `xs` be injective, and let `gs` be interpolation-eligible. The default construction uses `interpolationSupportSubset gs hEligible`; for every selected index $i$ it satisfies
--
--   $$
--   \left(\operatorname{restrictAtHeight}\left(\operatorname{interpolateCompletedSlices}(\mathrm{params},k,xs,gs),xs(i)\right)\right).\operatorname{poly}=\left((gs(i)).\operatorname{get}(\ldots)\right).\operatorname{poly}.
--   $$
--
--   The support-selection and Lagrange identities therefore recover each selected completed-slice polynomial.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.interpolateCompletedSlices_restrictAtHeight_eq_get_of_mem_supportSubset`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
